WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.502 --> 00:00:10.182
What's going on, Gavin?

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:13.227
Eritrea for a trip

00:00:13.966 --> 00:00:15.933
and this is...

00:00:16.342 --> 00:00:18.408
Well it's been
quite a journey already actually.

00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:19.791
Went to the Berlin embassy.

00:00:19.791 --> 00:00:21.887
I went once, you went what, three times?

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:24.070
I went four times.

00:00:24.287 --> 00:00:27.055
Four times and you got it
last minute, the last day.

00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:29.546
Literally last minute
after they told me I wasn't gonna get it.

00:00:29.546 --> 00:00:31.183
I was gonna do all sorts of shenanigans.

00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:34.062
I was gonna try to
get on this flight without a visa.

00:00:34.518 --> 00:00:36.072
WOMAN: Asmara.
PETER: Asmara?

00:00:36.655 --> 00:00:37.655
PETER: Okay.

00:00:39.058 --> 00:00:40.908
And this lady's been like a mother to me.

00:00:40.908 --> 00:00:43.228
She's amazing.
She gave me her bread at the airport

00:00:43.228 --> 00:00:45.369
and she's been very kind and gentle

00:00:45.369 --> 00:00:48.516
and given me nice smiles
and tried to give me more tea.

00:00:48.516 --> 00:00:52.937
And just all around,
a very cool, warm person.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:00.571
To be continued.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.611
Everyone has been super-rad so far.

00:01:02.611 --> 00:01:04.986
So many people just
come straight up to us.

00:01:04.986 --> 00:01:07.886
-Talk to us, tell us a story.
-Super friendly.

00:01:08.639 --> 00:01:10.899
They're pumped that
we're visiting their country.

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:12.579
Not as pumped as we are!

00:01:13.054 --> 00:01:14.574
♪ warm electronic ♪

00:01:58.115 --> 00:01:59.635
[music intensifies]

00:02:02.348 --> 00:02:03.628
[crowd cheering]

00:02:14.908 --> 00:02:16.348
[bicycles passing]

00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:25.547
♪ upbeat modern African ♪

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.715
[woman laughing]

00:02:49.321 --> 00:02:51.832
&lt;GAVIN: Say it again.
PETER: This guy said he's very strong.

00:02:51.832 --> 00:02:54.425
PETER: Let's see how strong he is.

00:02:55.748 --> 00:02:57.428
[bystanders laughing]

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.923
 [encouraging chatter]

00:03:00.958 --> 00:03:03.384
GAVIN: You got this, c'mon man!

00:03:04.782 --> 00:03:06.462
PETER: Up, up, up, up...

00:03:06.933 --> 00:03:08.133
GAVIN: Oh yeah.

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:09.887
[crowd cheering and laughing]

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:14.989
So in Eritrea when you
want to change money

00:03:15.542 --> 00:03:19.313
don't do it in the bank
because it's 15 to 1, the exchange rate

00:03:19.313 --> 00:03:20.993
and on the so called...

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:24.032
Whatever market you wanna call it

00:03:24.032 --> 00:03:26.056
it's 24 to 1.

00:03:26.056 --> 00:03:30.003
So it's the process of
getting bags of money

00:03:30.003 --> 00:03:31.803
and doing a lot of counting

00:03:32.321 --> 00:03:34.001
GAVIN: With the mafia.

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:37.566
I'm on the outskirts of Asmara

00:03:37.566 --> 00:03:40.327
and I've found quite an interesting place.

00:03:41.505 --> 00:03:45.030
Basically it is the resting point for all

00:03:45.731 --> 00:03:49.315
of these tanks, and trucks,
and military hardware from...

00:03:50.149 --> 00:03:54.228
I'm thinking from
the 30 year war here with Ethiopia.

00:03:54.228 --> 00:03:56.295
But it goes on, and on, and on.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.780
And...

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.237
It's an awesome site because

00:04:03.153 --> 00:04:04.633
I've never seen anything like it.

00:04:04.633 --> 00:04:06.515
It's also very depressing and...

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.527
Gross site of what humans...

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.901
Spend money on and do to each other.

00:04:15.398 --> 00:04:19.519
Day two...
Quite a really, really, fascinating find.

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:21.319
This city and this country.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:24.718
♪ upbeat modern African ♪

00:04:56.318 --> 00:04:58.451
[music fades into choir singing]

00:05:02.007 --> 00:05:04.167
This is a little bit different
to anywhere I've been

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.129
let alone Berlin.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:11.906
It's obvious from this beautiful picture
that we're not in Berlin.

00:05:11.906 --> 00:05:14.642
-Where are we, Gav?
-We're in Eritrea.

00:05:15.385 --> 00:05:16.965
We're about an hour from the capital

00:05:16.965 --> 00:05:19.032
in this place called Dekemhare.

00:05:19.398 --> 00:05:21.766
It's one of the most
chill places I've ever been.

00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:24.663
GAVIN: Woo.

00:05:24.663 --> 00:05:26.183
[children cheering]

00:05:30.409 --> 00:05:32.526
GAVIN: F*ckin' A, that was great.

00:05:32.804 --> 00:05:34.729
[children giggling]

00:05:42.336 --> 00:05:43.450
[children cheering]

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:44.965
Everyone's excited.

00:05:44.965 --> 00:05:47.411
[all cheering and laughing]

00:05:58.774 --> 00:06:00.294
[children cheering]

00:06:07.844 --> 00:06:09.577
PETER: One, two, three, go!

00:06:09.577 --> 00:06:11.708
[children yelling and cheering]

00:06:18.152 --> 00:06:20.310
[coffee shop chatter]

00:06:23.157 --> 00:06:24.890
[espresso machine hissing]

00:06:39.122 --> 00:06:40.594
Feeling quite ill

00:06:40.594 --> 00:06:44.743
but we're super lucky to get on this bus.

00:06:44.743 --> 00:06:46.201
It's the only one going to a city

00:06:46.201 --> 00:06:48.935
and we got it before it got the bus stop.

00:06:50.223 --> 00:06:51.223
[grunting]

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:59.953
It's more than a handshake,
it's a shoulder bumper.

00:07:00.312 --> 00:07:01.312
Brother...

00:07:03.268 --> 00:07:04.334
One more time.

00:07:04.491 --> 00:07:05.491
[grunting]

00:07:07.992 --> 00:07:08.992
GAVIN: Zopo!

00:07:10.334 --> 00:07:11.774
[Gavin chuckling]

00:07:17.244 --> 00:07:19.599
In the city of Massawa, the old city here

00:07:19.599 --> 00:07:22.032
and it's...

00:07:23.206 --> 00:07:25.940
It's beautiful but it's sort of in ruins.

00:07:26.619 --> 00:07:29.372
Old Ottoman architecture.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.540
And...

00:07:34.138 --> 00:07:38.084
Most other countries,
this would be a big tourist draw

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.436
but in Eritrea...

00:07:41.225 --> 00:07:42.225
Well...

00:07:42.844 --> 00:07:43.844
Not so much...

00:07:44.879 --> 00:07:45.879
Because...

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:48.521
Well, there are hardly any tourists here.

00:07:48.521 --> 00:07:49.721
There's like...

00:07:50.228 --> 00:07:53.748
I think we've seen
in 10 days maybe like...

00:07:54.627 --> 00:07:55.943
six white people.

00:07:55.943 --> 00:07:57.543
Something like that.

00:07:58.957 --> 00:08:02.345
Really, really an
off the beaten path type place.

00:08:02.345 --> 00:08:04.479
So check this out, this is cool.

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:06.812
♪ African pop music in the background ♪

00:08:10.469 --> 00:08:13.060
And people are just living in this.

00:08:13.633 --> 00:08:14.633
In this old city.

00:08:14.633 --> 00:08:15.633
And it's...

00:08:16.098 --> 00:08:19.029
I think it got hammered
pretty hard in the war.

00:08:19.029 --> 00:08:22.426
That's why it's all beat up but...

00:08:24.182 --> 00:08:27.044
Yeah, really, really interesting place.

00:08:28.652 --> 00:08:30.750
And the situation is
we're about to go into Sweets.

00:08:30.793 --> 00:08:33.820
We've been thinking about Sweets for days,
even you, Gavin Hamilton.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.700
Who doesn't have
a massive sweet tooth like me

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.857
has been talking
about this place for days.

00:08:38.857 --> 00:08:41.098
Why? They have amazing desserts.

00:08:41.698 --> 00:08:43.964
[Peter talking to staff inaudibly]

00:08:44.914 --> 00:08:46.274
[Gavin chuckling]

00:08:49.898 --> 00:08:50.898
[claps]

00:08:51.769 --> 00:08:52.769
Yes.

00:08:53.103 --> 00:08:55.826
Talk to the people.
Talk to the people, Mare.

00:08:55.826 --> 00:08:57.513
Nice to meet you, Peter.

00:08:57.513 --> 00:09:00.614
And your friends, hi to everybody.

00:09:00.614 --> 00:09:01.883
Come Eritrea.

00:09:02.725 --> 00:09:04.786
Why should they come to Asmara?

00:09:04.786 --> 00:09:10.413
Because it is
very beautiful city like London.

00:09:10.851 --> 00:09:11.854
[Peter chuckles]

00:09:11.854 --> 00:09:13.548
It's like London but different.

00:09:13.548 --> 00:09:15.103
But I'll say the people are nicer.

00:09:15.103 --> 00:09:16.934
-Yeah.
-People are friendlier, like Mare.

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:21.039
Everybody's gentle and we are fun.

00:09:21.039 --> 00:09:22.639
They give you peace.

00:09:24.441 --> 00:09:25.488
[hands slap]

00:09:25.488 --> 00:09:26.688
[both laughing]

00:09:26.688 --> 00:09:28.488
♪ upbeat tropical African ♪

